# wisp

> **WISP Isn't STUN Protocol**

a smol PoC for moving files over the internet using only the **mainline dht** and **tcp**

emphasis on **only**

no stun
no turn
no webrtc
no signaling server
no random cloud service or 3rd party

the dht is for finding peers
after that its just tcp doing tcp things

## why

because i wanted to see if it could be done
thats kind of it

## more on wisp

this is **not** trying to replace croc

or magic wormhole
or syncthing
or tailscale
or literally anything else

if youre looking for something that isnt broken go use one of those
this is a PoC

## but what about nat traversal

wisp doesnt do stun because *wisp isnt stun protocol*

if two peers cant make a tcp connection then youre probably not transferring anything today
that is NOT a bug and will NOT be fixed

